1
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:17,379
Calm down. Just calm down, okay?

2
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:18,579
The fixtures are all off-brand.

3
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:20,039
The plaster is hollow and a total mess.

4
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:22,260
The gaps in the floor are wide enough to fit a person.

5
00:00:22,339 --> 00:00:24,239
You call this the standard for a fully furnished place?

6
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:26,000
I thought I'd walked into a refugee camp.

7
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:29,660
The nearest market is five kilometers away.

8
00:00:29,899 --> 00:00:30,839
The roads aren't even paved.

9
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:32,560
You have to drive on dirt roads.

10
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:33,600
And when you finally get out of the car,

11
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:34,759
your shoes get covered in mud.

12
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:40,479
Ma Du.

13
00:00:40,759 --> 00:00:42,119
The keys are right here.

14
00:00:44,119 --> 00:00:44,759
Here.

15
00:00:44,939 --> 00:00:46,119
I see it, Tingting.

16
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:47,200
Careful now.

17
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:48,399
Let's go this way.

18
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:49,640
I'll move our things in.

19
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:50,700
Coming.

20
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:53,840
One, two, three.

21
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:57,579
We finally have our own home.

22
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:15,200
Could you two please

23
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,840
just put the apartment number up?

24
00:01:17,879 --> 00:01:19,859
Three, two, one.

25
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:21,879
Welcome home.

26
00:01:45,519 --> 00:01:47,920
That day was supposed to end normally.

27
00:01:48,159 --> 00:01:48,980
He got off work,

28
00:01:49,079 --> 00:01:50,799
went back to his newly renovated home,

29
00:01:51,099 --> 00:01:51,879
played on his phone,

30
00:01:51,959 --> 00:01:53,159
and checked the weather for the day

31
00:01:53,159 --> 00:01:54,239
his wife was coming back.

32
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:55,659
But by the time he came to his senses,

33
00:01:55,739 --> 00:01:56,879
it was already too late.

34
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:58,099
I do believe,

35
00:01:58,439 --> 00:02:00,659
I believe he might have acted on impulse.

36
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,280
But one wrong step,

37
00:02:02,859 --> 00:02:04,379
and you have no choice but to keep

38
00:02:04,439 --> 00:02:05,620
going down the wrong path.

39
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:08,759
Unless you can get him to confess on his own.

40
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:10,000
You're talking absolute bullshit.

41
00:02:10,060 --> 00:02:10,780
Get out.

42
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:11,240
I said,

43
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:11,919
get the hell out!

44
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:12,740
Calm down first. Get out!

45
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:14,000
I know you heard what I said.

46
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:14,699
Get out!

47
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:15,500
Listen,

48
00:02:16,419 --> 00:02:17,219
I'm warning you.

49
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,539
If you keep talking nonsense

50
00:02:18,539 --> 00:02:19,379
and harassing my family,

51
00:02:19,479 --> 00:02:20,620
I will definitely call the cops.

52
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:21,639
You...

53
00:02:21,719 --> 00:02:23,520
Calm down and think about what I said, okay?

54
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:25,539
Don't wait until it's past the point of no return.

55
00:02:25,879 --> 00:02:27,400
You'll figure it out, right?

56
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:28,699
You'll definitely figure it out.

57
00:02:29,219 --> 00:02:29,879
You...

58
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:46,180
But how can you be sure

59
00:02:46,659 --> 00:02:48,620
that you know everything about him?

60
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,419
I just got back and you want to sleep in separate rooms.

61
00:02:50,639 --> 00:02:52,099
No, I don't.

62
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:54,740
I don't want to, either.

63
00:02:54,919 --> 00:02:55,819
It's just...

64
00:02:56,979 --> 00:02:59,139
there never seems to be enough time.

65
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:01,139
I saw it with my own eyes.

66
00:03:01,379 --> 00:03:03,340
He bought two of everything

67
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:05,539
and put them into two separate bags.

68
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,280
Welcome home.

69
00:03:09,379 --> 00:03:10,280
You're back.

70
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:12,539
Just bring it over here.

71
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,479
Where are you taking that bag?

72
00:03:20,659 --> 00:03:21,599
Bring it here.

73
00:03:25,879 --> 00:03:26,800
You bought so much.

74
00:03:29,139 --> 00:03:29,919
Ma Du.

75
00:03:30,659 --> 00:03:31,419
Come here.

76
00:03:35,419 --> 00:03:36,219
What's wrong?

77
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:38,340
Are you hiding something from me?

78
00:03:43,319 --> 00:03:44,139
No.

79
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:46,060
What could I possibly be hiding from you?

80
00:03:52,139 --> 00:03:53,199
When was this delivered?

81
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:56,039
A... a few days ago.

82
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:58,819
Why didn't you tell me anything?

83
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:01,319
You've grown bold.

84
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:12,819
The walls in this entire house...

85
00:04:12,819 --> 00:04:14,219
we repainted all of them ourselves.

86
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:15,139
And the bathroom floor...

87
00:04:15,139 --> 00:04:16,019
we got down on our hands and knees

88
00:04:16,019 --> 00:04:17,699
and scrubbed it clean bit by bit.

89
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,920
We just bought a new bed for the bedroom, too.

90
00:04:20,019 --> 00:04:21,420
We signed a three-year lease!

91
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:22,360
Why does he just get to say he's selling

92
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:23,399
and we have to move out?

93
00:04:23,459 --> 00:04:24,180
Look, lady,

94
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:25,980
this is his house.

95
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:28,180
Besides, didn't he agree to compensate you?

96
00:04:28,639 --> 00:04:29,500
If you think it's not enough,

97
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:30,480
just say so.

98
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:32,019
It's not about the money!

99
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:33,220
Do you know how much effort

100
00:04:33,259 --> 00:04:34,779
we put into fixing this place up?

101
00:04:34,819 --> 00:04:35,860
Look around for yourself!

102
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:36,959
Everything in here...

103
00:04:37,079 --> 00:04:37,860
Tingting, Tingting.

104
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,300
What's wrong? What's going on here?

105
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:40,139
Look,

106
00:04:40,339 --> 00:04:41,139
just ask her.

107
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:47,579
Brother,

108
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:48,699
have a smoke. Here.

109
00:04:48,759 --> 00:04:49,980
You're too kind.

110
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,699
Alright, just tell me what's on your mind.

111
00:04:52,939 --> 00:04:53,980
As you can see,

112
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:56,100
my wife is pregnant.

113
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:58,759
And it's already the end of the year.

114
00:04:58,899 --> 00:05:01,100
Making us move at a time like this...

115
00:05:01,139 --> 00:05:03,240
Where am I supposed to find a place?

116
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:04,959
How about this?

117
00:05:05,439 --> 00:05:06,720
It's not that we won't move.

118
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:08,800
Can you give us a few more days?

119
00:05:08,899 --> 00:05:10,540
Even just a month.

120
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,560
We need time to look for a place.

121
00:05:12,639 --> 00:05:13,480
Please. I'm begging you.

122
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:15,879
I understand everything you're saying.

123
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:18,079
But it's no use telling me.

124
00:05:18,339 --> 00:05:19,920
I'm just an employee.

125
00:05:20,939 --> 00:05:21,819
Our landlord...

126
00:05:21,939 --> 00:05:23,300
is about the same age as us.

127
00:05:23,439 --> 00:05:25,399
But he's got his parents backing him up.

128
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:28,079
I know it's not fair.

129
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:30,360
But what can we do?

130
00:05:30,579 --> 00:05:31,360
With this sort of thing,

131
00:05:31,779 --> 00:05:33,439
you just have to accept it.

132
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:01,120
Take a break if you're tired.

133
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:12,600
It'll be okay.

134
00:06:14,259 --> 00:06:16,160
We'll have a home of our own.

135
00:06:19,639 --> 00:06:21,240
We'll have a home of our own.

136
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:24,319
Don't be scared.

137
00:06:24,879 --> 00:06:25,920
It'll all pass.

138
00:06:28,139 --> 00:06:28,959
We'll see ourselves out.

139
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:30,399
We're heading out.

140
00:06:32,839 --> 00:06:34,019
Is everything okay?

141
00:06:34,439 --> 00:06:35,360
Everything's fine.

142
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:36,819
Didn't Dr. Wang just...

143
00:06:36,879 --> 00:06:38,199
...tell you himself?

144
00:06:38,779 --> 00:06:39,699
It's nothing.

145
00:06:39,839 --> 00:06:41,019
You don't have to hide it from me.

146
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,680
There's really nothing wrong.

147
00:06:43,579 --> 00:06:44,779
We were just...

148
00:06:44,959 --> 00:06:46,019
...catching up.

149
00:06:46,399 --> 00:06:47,500
We haven't seen each other in ages.

150
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:49,079
And we bothered him again today.

151
00:06:49,459 --> 00:06:52,019
He said I'm probably just tired from the move.

152
00:06:52,639 --> 00:06:53,699
I'm fine.

153
00:06:53,899 --> 00:06:54,740
Really.

154
00:07:10,459 --> 00:07:11,779
Welcome home.

155
00:07:17,139 --> 00:07:18,079
I'm home.

156
00:07:28,279 --> 00:07:29,339
Come give me a hand!

157
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:38,240
Ma Du.

158
00:07:39,639 --> 00:07:41,000
Is anything wrong lately?

159
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:42,899
Nothing. What could possibly be wrong?

160
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:47,699
You can tell me anything.

161
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:54,540
You don't have to keep things from me.

162
00:07:58,199 --> 00:07:59,060
Nothing's wrong.

163
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:00,779
Really.

164
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,959
What could possibly be wrong with me?

165
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:05,360
Stop overthinking it.

166
00:10:34,460 --> 00:10:35,340
Stop obsessing over it.

167
00:10:35,419 --> 00:10:36,820
Okay, okay. We're gonna be late.

168
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:37,879
Let's go, let's go, let's go.

169
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:39,139
Be careful on the road.

170
00:12:00,519 --> 00:12:01,700
I have no idea

171
00:12:01,879 --> 00:12:04,019
how things ended up like this.

172
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:07,620
It's like...

173
00:12:08,980 --> 00:12:10,980
it's like a dream.

174
00:13:05,539 --> 00:13:07,299
Time's up. Pens down.

175
00:13:08,659 --> 00:13:09,980
Excuse me, stop writing.

176
00:13:17,799 --> 00:13:20,220
I said, stop writing.

177
00:14:13,639 --> 00:14:14,320
Huanhuan.

178
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:15,159
Look at Mommy.

179
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:16,139
Look at Mommy.

180
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:17,480
Let Daddy see.

181
00:14:17,519 --> 00:14:18,919
You've learned to lift your head!

182
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:21,919
Good job, Huanhuan.

183
00:14:22,399 --> 00:14:23,840
Do you want to see Daddy soon?

184
00:15:04,639 --> 00:15:05,600
How can this be?

185
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:06,919
How can this be?

186
00:15:11,559 --> 00:15:12,600
Pupils aren't dilated.

187
00:15:12,919 --> 00:15:14,279
Why can't I hear any heart sounds?

188
00:15:14,659 --> 00:15:15,799
It doesn't seem like a pneumothorax.

189
00:15:16,259 --> 00:15:17,600
Is it cardiac arrest?

190
00:15:18,940 --> 00:15:19,639
No.

191
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:21,399
No, it could also be...

192
00:15:21,759 --> 00:15:23,279
It could also be an aortic rupture.

193
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:24,399
Follow the protocol.

194
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:25,559
Follow the protocol.

195
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:26,879
Call for an ambulance first.

196
00:15:33,259 --> 00:15:34,519
At critical moments in life,

197
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,519
there's no room for error.

198
00:17:13,220 --> 00:17:14,599
Welcome home

199
00:18:30,119 --> 00:18:32,339
Are you home? Why didn't you reply?

200
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:38,740
I'm home.

201
00:18:39,619 --> 00:18:41,240
I worked overtime all day today.

202
00:18:41,279 --> 00:18:42,500
I'm exhausted.

203
00:18:42,539 --> 00:18:43,740
I just walked in.

204
00:18:43,900 --> 00:18:44,819
I'm sorry.

205
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:55,779
Based on what you just described,

206
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:58,539
your friend is involved in a hit-and-run,

207
00:18:58,779 --> 00:19:00,779
and potentially intentional homicide,

208
00:19:01,079 --> 00:19:03,019
depending on the victim's final condition.

209
00:19:03,259 --> 00:19:04,240
Your friend will face

210
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:05,859
three to seven years in prison.

211
00:19:06,119 --> 00:19:08,259
As for their tenure at a Grade 3A hospital,

212
00:19:08,519 --> 00:19:10,779
if convicted of a traffic offense,

213
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:11,559
according to regulations,

214
00:19:11,619 --> 00:19:12,859
they will generally be dismissed.

215
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:11,259
Sir, please fix this for me.

216
00:20:13,660 --> 00:20:14,339
Boss,

217
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:15,880
this isn't exactly a luxury car.

218
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:16,599
It's just a tiny dent.

219
00:20:16,599 --> 00:20:17,900
Why bother fixing it?

220
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:19,059
Sir.

221
00:20:19,779 --> 00:20:20,859
It's a friend's car.

222
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:22,180
As soon as possible.

223
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:29,519
Stop talking for a second.

224
00:20:29,519 --> 00:20:31,140
Just listen to me, okay?

225
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:33,299
I... let me confirm this with you again.

226
00:20:33,339 --> 00:20:34,460
You must, absolutely must

227
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:35,940
deliver it to me today.

228
00:20:36,180 --> 00:20:36,980
A ventilator,

229
00:20:37,079 --> 00:20:38,259
right, a suction machine,

230
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:40,339
a feeding tube, and IV drips.

231
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:41,259
And then...

232
00:20:46,579 --> 00:20:47,500
Um, I...

233
00:20:47,940 --> 00:20:49,059
I'll talk to you later.

234
00:20:50,140 --> 00:20:51,420
What... what's wrong, Lao Yang?

235
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:53,019
Did something happen to someone at home?

236
00:20:53,299 --> 00:20:54,660
Bring them to the hospital.

237
00:20:55,039 --> 00:20:56,619
Why set this up at home?

238
00:20:57,079 --> 00:20:58,299
The situation is a bit complicated.

239
00:20:58,539 --> 00:21:00,259
It's easier for me to care for them at home.

240
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:03,099
Just say the word if you need anything.

241
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:06,339
Don't shoulder it all by yourself.

242
00:21:06,420 --> 00:21:07,779
I'll definitely help you.

243
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:09,539
I'm a man of my word.

244
00:22:24,319 --> 00:22:24,980
Hello.

245
00:22:25,339 --> 00:22:27,460
Are you the owner of the car ending in 629?

246
00:22:28,019 --> 00:22:28,700
Yes, I am.

247
00:22:28,799 --> 00:22:30,640
We saw that in the early hours of the 4th,

248
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:31,740
you entered the parking garage.

249
00:22:31,940 --> 00:22:33,640
Did you come back via Fangxing Road that day,

250
00:22:33,700 --> 00:22:36,059
or the small road next to the complex?

251
00:22:36,220 --> 00:22:38,059
What day was the 4th?

252
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:39,779
The 4th was a Friday.

253
00:22:40,099 --> 00:22:41,579
I worked overtime on Friday.

254
00:22:42,019 --> 00:22:43,579
I took the small road back.

255
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:45,900
And when you passed through that small road,

256
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:47,779
did you see any pedestrians?

257
00:22:48,119 --> 00:22:48,859
No.

258
00:22:49,299 --> 00:22:50,579
That road

259
00:22:50,759 --> 00:22:51,460
is really deserted.

260
00:22:51,619 --> 00:22:52,480
Usually,

261
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:54,180
only people driving take that route.

262
00:22:55,839 --> 00:22:56,500
All right.

263
00:22:56,819 --> 00:22:57,859
Thank you for your cooperation.

264
00:22:57,980 --> 00:22:59,140
You're welcome. Glad to help.

265
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:00,460
Let's go.

266
00:23:20,019 --> 00:23:22,819
I've got good news and bad news.

267
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:23,980
Which do you want to hear first?

268
00:23:28,579 --> 00:23:30,259
The bad news is,

269
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:32,880
that old witch is making me go back to work,

270
00:23:33,079 --> 00:23:35,019
viciously tearing me and my son apart.

271
00:23:35,559 --> 00:23:37,160
The good news is,

272
00:23:37,220 --> 00:23:38,619
your precious wife

273
00:23:38,619 --> 00:23:40,940
will be right back by your side.

274
00:23:42,180 --> 00:23:44,339
My mom gave me two huge bags of sweet potato noodles,

275
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:46,339
saying it's enough to last us a whole year.

276
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:07,740
Tingting.

277
00:24:07,779 --> 00:24:08,740
What are you doing?

278
00:24:08,839 --> 00:24:10,180
Why are you just now picking up?

279
00:24:10,339 --> 00:24:12,819
I was writing my paper. I didn't hear it.

280
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:15,059
Aren't you excited to hear that I'm coming back?

281
00:24:15,680 --> 00:24:16,740
How could I not be?

282
00:24:16,740 --> 00:24:18,740
You... you have no idea how much I miss you.

283
00:24:18,819 --> 00:24:19,579
I don't believe you.

284
00:24:19,900 --> 00:24:21,059
Are you hiding someone at home?

285
00:24:21,119 --> 00:24:21,940
Let me see.

286
00:24:22,660 --> 00:24:23,180
I...

287
00:24:29,299 --> 00:24:30,059
Tingting.

288
00:24:32,259 --> 00:24:32,900
I...

289
